---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---
<PageLayout
  title="Privacy Choices and Deletion"
  seoTitle="Remove App Photo Copies and Other Privacy Choices"
  description="How to remove Golden Moments photo copies without deleting your original photos, check device backups and ask us to delete information we hold."
  path="/privacy-choices/"
  crumb="Privacy choices"
  updated="2026-10-25"
  lede="You can stop, remove a copy or delete the app. Your original photos are separate and stay where they are."
>
  <aside class="notice" aria-labelledby="choices-summary">
    <div>
      <strong id="choices-summary">Two things to know first</strong>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Removing a photo in Golden Moments does not delete the original</strong> from your photo library.</li>
        <li><strong>Removing the app’s copies does not erase earlier backups</strong> or copies you sent to someone else. Manage those separately.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </aside>
  <p>You can play the included activities without adding family photos or creating an account.</p>

  <h2 id="remove-one">Remove one photo</h2>
  <p>In version 1.4.0 and later:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Open Golden Moments and choose <strong>Your family photos</strong>.</li>
    <li>Find the photo and choose <strong>Options</strong>.</li>
    <li>Choose <strong>Remove this copy</strong>, read the message and choose <strong>Remove copy</strong>.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    This removes the app’s working copy, not your original. If you do not see <strong>Your family photos</strong>, your
    installed version does not include family photos.
  </p>

  <h2 id="remove-all">Remove all photo copies</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Open <strong>Your family photos</strong>.</li>
    <li>Choose <strong>Remove all photo copies</strong>, then <strong>Remove all copies</strong>.</li>
    <li>If an error appears, try again or <a href="/support/">contact support</a> with a description. Please do not send the photos.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Removing the app’s copies does not change your photo library, your cloud photo library or earlier device backups.</p>

  <h2 id="delete-app">Delete the app and its data</h2>
  <p>
    On iPhone or iPad, use <strong>Delete App</strong> and confirm. This normally removes the app and the data it keeps
    on the device. <strong>Offload App</strong> is different: it can keep the app’s documents and data so they come back
    when you reinstall.
  </p>
  <p>
    On Android, uninstall Golden Moments or clear its storage in the device’s app settings. Menus differ between device
    makers. Clearing data cannot be undone, so save anything you want to keep first.
  </p>
  <p>We cannot erase anything on your device remotely, because Golden Moments has no user accounts or photo server.</p>

  <h2 id="backups">Backups, iCloud and other copies</h2>
  <p>
    iCloud, Google, device maker or computer backups may contain app data, depending on your settings. Removing
    something in the app, or deleting the app, does not automatically delete copies from earlier backups. Check your
    device’s backup settings and the device maker’s guidance before removing a backup, especially if it protects other
    important information.
  </p>
  <p>If you shared a photo with another person or app, that copy is theirs to manage. We cannot recall or erase it.</p>

  <h2 id="permissions">Photo access</h2>
  <p>
    Adding photos is optional, and the app uses only the photos you select. You can change photo permissions in your
    device’s Settings. Turning off permission does not remove copies already added; use the steps above.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Ask about information we hold</h2>
  <p>
    If you emailed support, we may have your email address and message. To ask for access, correction or deletion, or to
    withdraw consent where that applies, email
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}?subject=Golden%20Moments%20privacy%20request`}>{SITE.supportEmail}</a> and say
    what you would like us to find. We may ask for a little information to confirm the request is yours, and the law may
    require us to keep some records.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Please do not send medical records, a diagnosis, identity documents or photos with your request.</strong>
    We cannot reach or delete anything that is only on your device or in another company’s account.
  </p>
  <p>
    Read the full <a href="/app-privacy/">app privacy policy</a>. The <a href="/privacy/">website privacy notice</a>
    covers this website.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
